{
  "_note": "Translates each rn5 taxiway-file stem (DCS's internal AirfieldsTaxiways filename, sometimes cryptic/legacy) to that airbase's canonical name. buildAirportPolygons.js/airportPolygonsCore.js use this value as the join key into the matching client/public/runways/<Theatre>.json's 'airbase' field to attach real runway coordinates to the stem's taxiway polygons; Login.jsx's resolveIcao expects the same canonical name to match the live DCS callsign. The value must be that SAME physical airbase's own real name — never a different, unrelated airbase's name borrowed just because no runway JSON entry exists for this one (that stitches one airbase's taxiways to a different airbase's runway; see the Zarqa/Muwaffaq Salti bug this note followed from, two real airbases ~60km apart in Syria that got wrongly aliased together). If a stem's airbase genuinely has no runway JSON entry, map it to itself (identity) — its taxiway/polygon data still gets sourced and rendered fine, it just won't be a selectable login facility until DCS exposes real runway data for it (see icaoMapping.json's note).",

